        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Anna Maria, Florida; Anna Maria Island; Bradenton Beach, Florida; Manatee County, Florida; Longboat Key\n- Concepts: municipal geography; island boundaries\n\nFacts:\n- Anna Maria, Florida, is a city in Manatee County, Florida, United States.\n- Anna Maria, Florida, occupies the northern part of Anna Maria Island.\n- Anna Maria, Florida, is one of three municipalities on Anna Maria Island.\n- Anna Maria Island is bounded on the west by the Gulf of Mexico.\n- Anna Maria Island is bounded on the south by Longboat Pass, which separates it from Longboat Key.\n- Anna Maria Island is bounded on the east by Anna Maria Sound.\n- Anna Maria Island is bounded on the north by Tampa Bay.\n- Bradenton Beach, Florida, is a city on Anna Maria Island in Manatee County, Florida, United States.",
